<title>INDIA: Indian soybean firmer on slow arrivals.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean firmer on slow arrivals.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices were up by around 100 rupees per tonne in central Indian markets on poor arrivals.</p>
<p>The undertone was firm despite low trading volume.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices remained bearish on poor demand against increased supplies. Soyoil solvent was down by 200 rupees and soyoil refined was down by 100 rupees per tonne today. Business was dull and the undertone was easy.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were slightly up on limited offerings from Indian exporters. Soymeal yellow was $260-262 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) west coast Indian ports for export. Rapeseed extraction was $94-95 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) in bulk for export and was 3,250-3,275 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on rail) condition. Business volume was dull and the undertone was steady.</p>
